#: ../guide/walk_forward.md:89 cf460ed7521549bfa0d638c8ce9e7716
msgid "A typical workflow"
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/walk_forward.md:125 38b88c403b154537a42fbd0bef01a85f
msgid ""
"If the in-sample Sharpe and OoS mean are wildly different, you've found "
"your overfit. The OoS number is the one to trust."
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/walk_forward.md:128 48664a1f27124c30a7b650615055df1f
msgid "Choosing the windows"
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/walk_forward.md:130 cf4e8429a84a4d8ba4ef9be5296581e1
msgid "The right `train_window` and `test_window` depend on:"
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/walk_forward.md:132 98869032a26e4875ab525bdbaf27eb22
msgid ""
"**Strategy \"memory\"**: how many bars does the strategy need to fit a "
"parameter? A 20-bar SMA needs at least ~50 bars to give the system some "
"room. A 200-bar lookback model needs a much larger train_window."
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/walk_forward.md:135 f308095b0a984277904e550442477454
msgid ""
"**Market regime length**: a train window that's too small only sees one "
"regime; too large straddles multiple regimes (averaging conflicting "
"optima). 6–12 months of daily bars is a typical starting point."
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/walk_forward.md:138 ac35969c2fe34cf9839ada2301625534
msgid ""
"**Number of windows you can afford**: longer windows = fewer windows, but"
" more data per fit; shorter windows = more windows but each is noisier. "
"Aim for **at least 5–10 windows** so the summary statistics are "
"meaningful."
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/walk_forward.md:143 810f520229474ec890ca4bc727417157
msgid "Rule of thumb: `train_window ≈ 4–10 × test_window` is a common ratio."
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/walk_forward.md:145 5e74dc9672824d23b3669f7e6b621fe4
msgid "Common pitfalls"
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/walk_forward.md:147 1516f12bc6c4402fb056f3eac993b01b
msgid "\"OoS hit rate is 0.5\""
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/walk_forward.md:149 e22bc53ba0b242b585a8a0b35ae6ac24
msgid ""
"Coin flip. Either the strategy genuinely doesn't have edge, or your "
"parameter grid doesn't cover the meaningful space. Try:"
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/walk_forward.md:152 4c0e1b53c5d84a278a4cc0f3407e1540
msgid ""
"Look at *which* params win in each window — if they're wildly different "
"across windows, the strategy isn't stable."
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/walk_forward.md:154 298f42ef73df44d3a3a2e3d68bd1173a
msgid ""
"Widen the grid. If the optimum keeps landing at the edge, you're not "
"exploring far enough."
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/walk_forward.md:156 74cf87d2aa99418491939ee1cc29bfac
msgid "Try a longer `train_window`."
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/walk_forward.md:158 53ae793c7614425a883dd086d3a1ed07
msgid "\"Mean OoS return is positive but min is catastrophic\""
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/walk_forward.md:160 e1d20e71c38846c6a1bdf937f9f372bf
msgid ""
"A common signature of strategies that work most of the time but blow up "
"periodically (e.g. martingale-like betting, undefended short vol). The "
"mean hides the tail."
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/walk_forward.md:164 5924011ea84c44dd869042afbe533d99
msgid "Always look at the per-window list, not just the summary."
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/walk_forward.md:166 44dfe04fc90548f8bbf6c1434d6745a6
msgid "\"Walk-forward Sharpe is much lower than in-sample Sharpe\""
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/walk_forward.md:168 6187fe03261a447f80ddf4f4b76fb514
msgid ""
"Expected and normal. The gap is your overfit. A 2:1 ratio (in-sample 2.0 "
"→ OoS 1.0) is fine; 5:1 means you're fitting noise. Reduce parameter "
"freedom (smaller grid) or extend the strategy's inductive bias (use a "
"constraint, share parameters across assets, etc.)."
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/walk_forward.md:173 a39bb5f583b7444ca7daa94577d65289
msgid "\"Step smaller than test_window\""
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/walk_forward.md:175 f2fca09fbb55417f82dcd004686ec6b6
msgid ""
"This produces *overlapping* test windows. The summary metrics double-"
"count bars and inflate `n_windows`. Sometimes you want this (e.g. for "
"adaptive walk-forward that retrains weekly), but understand that the "
"windows aren't statistically independent."
msgstr ""

